"""Publish measured advanced-fusion results without reliability overclaims."""
import html
import json
from pathlib import Path
from neurofusion.data import save_json
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];out=root/'experiments/advanced-fusion-001'
r=json.loads((out/'summary.json').read_text())
rows=[]
for name,v in r['modes'].items():
    c=v['calibration'];a=v['abstention']
    rows.append(f'<tr><td>{name}</td><td>{v["members"]}</td><td>{v["mean_dice"]:.4f}</td><td>{v["mean_absolute_volume_error_ml"]:.2f}</td><td>{v["lesions"]["lesion_recall"]:.3f}</td><td>{v["temperature"]}</td><td>{c["raw"]["mean"]["nll"]:.5f} / {c["calibrated"]["mean"]["nll"]:.5f}</td><td>{a["coverage"]:.1%}</td><td>{sum(v["development_checks"].values())}/5</td></tr>')
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Advanced fusion evaluation</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1200px;margin:30px auto;padding:20px;background:#101e2c;color:#eee}a{color:#80ded0}td,th{padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #567;text-align:left}.scroll{overflow:auto}</style><a href="/">Workspace</a><h1>Advanced fusion: development evaluation</h1><p>Separate DWI/ADC encoders with modality-dropout training. Equal-weight available-member ensemble; single-member ADC-only fallback has no ensemble-disagreement estimate. Both inputs missing is rejected.</p><p>Final epoch 5; 174 training and 37 development validation patients. Calibration fit/evaluation partition: 18/19 patients, reused from development. No holdout or UCSF inference. No active model replaced.</p><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Available inputs</th><th>Members</th><th>Dice</th><th>Volume error mL</th><th>Lesion recall</th><th>Temperature</th><th>NLL raw / calibrated</th><th>Retained coverage</th><th>Checks</th></tr>'''+''.join(rows)+'</table></div><h2>Individual member Dice</h2><ul>'+''.join('<li>'+html.escape(k)+f': {v:.4f}</li>' for k,v in r['member_mean_dice'].items())+'</ul><h2>Interpretation</h2><p>Entropy and disagreement are research uncertainty signals, not probabilities of diagnostic correctness. Reliability has not been independently established. Every failed calibration or abstention check is retained in the full results. Missing-input results simulate removal from aligned pairs, rather than testing a new missing-input clinical population. Brain-support voxel metrics may hide poor small-lesion performance.</p><p><a href="summary.json">All checks and case results</a> · <a href="protocol.json">Recorded protocol</a> · <a href="checkpoint-reproduction.json">Checkpoint reproduction</a></p></html>'
(out/'index.html').write_text(page,encoding='utf-8')
decision='<section><h2>Acceptance decision: not qualified</h2><p>ADC-only yielded zero Dice on all 37 cases. Its five aggregate uncertainty checks passing does not demonstrate useful segmentation or reliable uncertainty. ADC-only execution is disabled in the experimental inference command. Both-input and DWI-only ensembles remain below the DWI baseline on mean Dice; full-input calibration fails Brier/ECE and DWI-only calibration fails ECE. No calibrator, abstention rule or fusion model is promoted.</p></section>'
(out/'index.html').write_text(page.replace('</html>',decision+'</html>'),encoding='utf-8')
lines=['# Advanced fusion development experiment','','Separate-encoder fusion, equal-weight ensembles, simulated missing-input inference, and patient-partitioned calibration/abstention evaluation are implemented. Independent reliability and deployment qualification remain unestablished.','','| Mode | Dice | Volume error mL | Uncertainty checks |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for mode,v in r['modes'].items():
    lines.append(f'| {mode} | {v["mean_dice"]:.4f} | {v["mean_absolute_volume_error_ml"]:.3f} | {sum(v["development_checks"].values())}/5 |')
lines+=['','## Scope','Five epochs, seed 42, 174 training patients, 37 validation patients. Separate encoder has 105,105 parameters versus 91,417 DWI-only and 91,633 early-fusion parameters; this is not a capacity-matched causal ablation. Final epoch selected before training. Calibration temperatures and abstention cutoff fitted on 18 validation patients, assessed on 19 different validation patients. These are reused development data, not independent evaluation. Each availability pattern has its own fitted temperature and cutoff.','', 'Unavailable encoders are gated; modality absence is explicit. DWI-only uses DWI baseline plus separate encoder; ADC-only uses the separate encoder alone and does not emit ensemble variance. Both missing rejects. Malformed or misaligned supplied inputs must be rejected, never silently treated as missing. Missing-DWI evaluation uses the paired DWI reference grid and support, which limits its applicability to standalone ADC inputs.','','All three complete-input checkpoints are replayed on every validation patient. Native-grid probabilities, entropy and multi-member variance are saved under experiments/advanced-fusion-001/evaluation. Entropy is not calibrated error probability. Do not use a low uncertainty value as proof of health.','','## Evidence','- experiments/advanced-fusion-001/protocol.json','- experiments/advanced-fusion-001/summary.json','- experiments/advanced-fusion-001/checkpoint-reproduction.json','- experiments/separate-encoder-001/coverage-verification.json','','No model promotion or independent test inference occurred. Original baselines remain active.']
lines += ['', '## Acceptance decision', 'Not qualified. ADC-only produced zero Dice on all 37 cases despite passing the aggregate uncertainty checks. This demonstrates that those checks cannot establish usable segmentation or clinical reliability. Both-input and DWI-only ensembles underperform the DWI baseline on mean Dice. Both-input calibration fails Brier/ECE; DWI-only calibration fails ECE. All results are preserved. No model/calibrator/abstention rule is promoted.', '', '## Experimental local inference', 'Run `.venv-neurofusion/Scripts/python.exe scripts/predict_advanced_fusion.py --dwi PATH --adc PATH --output FRESH_DIRECTORY`. ADC is optional; DWI is required because ADC-only failed evaluation and is disabled. Malformed data, conflicting orientation forms or mismatched physical grids reject. This CLI writes raw probability, entropy and multi-member variance maps; it does not apply calibration or make abstention/clinical decisions. Keep provisional independent-evaluation cases out of this command.']
(root/'docs/ADVANCED_FUSION.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
print('Published advanced fusion report and documentation')
